{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01Ftab3NgX98Jg8cxidbtQ6G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. **Q22: Citations and source attribution in RAG** is written and committed.\n\nKey content in the answer:\n- **Metadata-at-ingestion** — chunk metadata (doc_id, page, section, URL) captured at index time and passed through every stage\n- **Numbered source blocks** — `[1] (policy-v3.pdf, p.7): \"...\"` injected into the generation prompt with explicit cite-by-index instruction\n- **Citation validation** — two-tier: fast string-overlap check + NLI entailment (DeBERTa, threshold 0.75) for high-stakes domains; catches ~4% hallucinated citations\n- **Structured JSON response** — `{ answer, citations: [{index, title, url, page}] }` so the frontend renders inline links\n- **Tradeoff**: string overlap (free, fast) vs NLI entailment (+80–200ms, catches paraphrased hallucinations)\n- **Pitfalls**: treating it as a prompt-only problem, skipping citation validation, returning raw `[1]` markers without structured metadata\n\nNext up: **Q23 — How does ANN search work? HNSW indexing?**"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":309,"cache_read_input_tokens":60160,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":309,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7919a165-b5ea-4202-bd62-173d4fed6171","uuid":"b10da954-d6c0-4d46-9134-09d6146f8673"}
